# "Torpedo" de la API REST de Flowable adaptado al proceso ventaMapuescuela.
# Basado en el ApiRestFlowable.http del ejemplo del curso (INP-complementario-socios).
# Se usa con la extensión "REST Client" de VS Code (humao.rest-client).

### Variables globales
@authorization = Basic rest-admin:test
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/flowable-rest

### 0) Salud del motor
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/management/engine
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json

### 1) Desplegar el modelo BPMN
POST {{baseUrl}}/service/repository/deployments
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="ventaMapuescuela.bpmn"
Content-Type: application/xml

< ../bpmn/ventaMapuescuela.bpmn
------Boundary--

### 2) Ver definiciones desplegadas (confirmar que ventaMapuescuela existe)
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/repository/process-definitions?key=ventaMapuescuela
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json

### 3) Iniciar una instancia (lo que hará la web en cada checkout)
# businessKey = número de pedido → permite encontrar la instancia desde la app
POST {{baseUrl}}/service/runtime/process-instances
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "processDefinitionKey": "ventaMapuescuela",
  "businessKey": "PED-0001",
  "variables": [
    { "name": "pedidoId",         "type": "integer", "value": 1 },
    { "name": "clienteNombre",    "value": "Juan Pérez" },
    { "name": "clienteEmail",     "value": "juan@example.com" },
    { "name": "montoTotal",       "type": "integer", "value": 15000 },
    { "name": "modalidadEntrega", "value": "RETIRO" },
    { "name": "plazoPago",        "value": "PT2M" }
  ]
}
# ↑ plazoPago PT2M solo para demos; en producción PT24H (viene de configuración)

### 4) Ver instancias en ejecución
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/runtime/process-instances
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json

### 5) Tareas activas de una instancia (¿dónde está el token?)
@processInstanceId = PEGAR-ID-AQUI
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/runtime/tasks?processInstanceId={{processInstanceId}}
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json

### 6) Completar "Adjuntar comprobante" (la web lo hace cuando el cliente sube el archivo)
@taskId = PEGAR-TASKID-AQUI
POST {{baseUrl}}/service/runtime/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "complete" }

### 7) Completar "Revisar comprobante" APROBANDO
POST {{baseUrl}}/service/runtime/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "complete",
  "variables": [
    { "name": "esAprobado", "type": "boolean", "value": true }
  ]
}

### 7b) Completar "Revisar comprobante" RECHAZANDO
POST {{baseUrl}}/service/runtime/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "complete",
  "variables": [
    { "name": "esAprobado",    "type": "boolean", "value": false },
    { "name": "motivoRechazo", "value": "El monto transferido no coincide" }
  ]
}

### 8) Variables de la instancia
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/runtime/process-instances/{{processInstanceId}}/variables
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json

### 9) Historial de actividades (el recorrido del token — evidencia para las demos)
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/history/historic-activity-instances?processInstanceId={{processInstanceId}}&sort=startTime&order=asc
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json

### 10) Timers programados (ver el job del plazo de 24h esperando)
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/management/timer-jobs
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json

### 11) External worker jobs pendientes (lo que consumirá el worker)
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/runtime/external-worker-jobs
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json

### 12) Jobs muertos (deadletter) y reintento
GET {{baseUrl}}/service/management/deadletter-jobs
Authorization: {{authorization}}
Accept: application/json
